# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. One line per moved URL: from, to, status.
#
# THIS IS NOT scripts/site/build_redirect.py, AND THE TWO ANSWER DIFFERENT HOSTS. That script
# generates a stub per page on the RETIRED github.io host, for links written before the move on
# 2026-08-10. This file forwards a URL that moved WITHIN this site, on the host serving it now.
# Neither one can do the other's job: the old host is not this project's deploy target, and this
# file is not served from it.
#
# A REAL 301 RATHER THAN A META-REFRESH STUB, which is the one place this improves on that script's
# reasoning. docs/assets/style.css allows a script only when "the answer it filtered was complete
# before any script ran", which is why the stubs carry a meta refresh AND a visible link. A rule
# here needs neither: the redirect is the HTTP response, so it is complete for a reader with
# JavaScript disabled, for a crawler, and for curl.
#
# /CHORUS was live from 01:33 on 2026-08-13 and was renamed to /KORUS at 15:06 the same day, in #48.
# It is named in #45, in this repository's history, and in anything anyone saved in those 13 hours.
/CHORUS     /KORUS     301
/CHORUS.md  /KORUS.md  301
